  "summary": "Traditional Japanese stencil patterns used for dyeing fabrics, particularly kimono.",
  "description": "Ise katagami features intricate geometric and nature-inspired designs with fine cut-out details, created for resist dyeing techniques. Developed in the Ise region, these stencils represent centuries of craftsmanship and technical precision in Japanese textile arts.",
  "culturalContext": "The use of stencils was known by the Nara period, as is evident from objects in the Shōsōin (正倉院). Later paper stencils developed alongside kimono. The technique is known as ise katagami since towns in Ise Province, now Mie Prefecture, were historic centres of the craft. Production is now primarily localised around the town of Suzuka.",
